# Identity

- End user = Knox JWT (`sub`, `knox.id`). Agent API keys are not CDP users.
- Agent platform = APISIX consumer (mTLS or caller key). Require both on partner traffic; Phase 1 may be JWT-only for curl tests.
- Authorization = Ranger via Knox. Forward the caller's bearer unchanged.

Validate Knox RS256 tokens (`iss=KNOXSSO`) with pinned JWKS or a configured public key. Do not use APISIX `jwt-auth` as the primary plugin.

```text
# ❌ BAD — second token format
jwt-auth issues an APISIX consumer JWT, then maps that to a Knox user

# ✅ GOOD — Knox bearer is the user credential
knox-jwt verifies the pinned Knox PEM (RS256, iss, exp, sub), then proxies Authorization
```

Never log the raw token. Pin JWKS to the inventory Knox host; ignore foreign `jku` URLs.
